# Copy to .env and adjust. Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_, and it
# inlines them at build time - so changing any of these needs a rebuild, and
# none of them may hold a secret. Everything below ends up readable in the
# published JavaScript, which is fine: they are all public identifiers.

# Where the backend is. 8001 if it is running in Docker, 8000 if you started
# uvicorn yourself.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001

# The site's own canonical origin, used for canonical URLs, og:url, the sitemap
# and the structured data. Leave unset locally: it defaults to production, and
# canonicals are only read by crawlers, which never see a dev build. Set it on a
# staging deploy so staging does not tell Google it is the original of every
# production page.
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://www.vproskills.com

# Google Search Console HTML-tag verification. Search Console > Settings >
# Ownership verification > HTML tag - the content= value only. DNS verification
# is better and does not need this. Leave unset until you have the token.
# VITE_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# --- Advertising measurement -------------------------------------------------
#
# All three are optional and all three are off by default. With none of them
# set, no tag is loaded, no request is made, and the consent notice does not
# appear - there would be nothing to consent to. That is the correct state for
# local development and for production until the ad accounts exist.
#
# When they are set, nothing still loads until the visitor accepts the notice.
# See web/src/analytics/tags.ts.

# Google Analytics 4. Admin > Data streams > your stream > Measurement ID.
# VITE_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Google Ads. Tools > Conversions - the tag ID, the AW- half.
# VITE_GOOGLE_ADS_ID=AW-000000000

# The label half of the conversion action, shown as "AW-000000000/AbC-D_efGh".
# Only the part after the slash goes here. Without it, Google Ads records page
# views but no conversions, so the campaign has nothing to optimise towards.
# VITE_GOOGLE_ADS_CONVERSION_LABEL=AbC-D_efGh

# Meta Pixel. Events Manager > Data sources > your pixel > Pixel ID.
# VITE_META_PIXEL_ID=000000000000000
